                        <h1>Careers &amp; Staff Directory</h1>
       <span id="d.en.14441"></span>
<div class="general-text">
  
  <p><span><img src="/media/fdtc/people/employment-opportunities/Employment-108482557.jpg" alt="An image of a signpost showing the way to employment and a career" style=" " /></span></p>
<p>Welcome to Florence-Darlington Technical College! Thank you for your interest in employment opportunities at FDTC. We&rsquo;re excited that you are considering FDTC, an equal-opportunity employer, to begin or continue your career.</p>
<p>As an employer with more than a 150-million-dollar economic impact on our service region, we take pride in our dedication to providing a high-quality education, promoting community service, and embracing professional development for our employees. We seek highly-qualified, passionate candidates who share in our core values of: Accountability, Excellence, Innovation, Integrity, Leadership, Teamwork, and Communication.</p>
<p>We endeavor to cultivate a community of compassionate professionals that are <strong>&ldquo;Student Focused.&rdquo;</strong></p>
</div><span id="d.en.19413"></span>
<div class="general-text">
  <h2>Why Join FDTC?</h2>
  <ul>
<li><strong>Competitive Compensation </strong>&ndash; We offer a competitive salary and benefits package to attract and retain talent.<br /><br /></li>
<li><strong>Work/Life Balance </strong>&ndash; Our work schedule is Monday through Thursday, 8:00 AM to 5:30 PM and Friday, 8:00 AM to 11:30 PM.<br /><br /></li>
<li><strong>Benefits</strong> &ndash; We offer health, dental, vision, prescription drug programs, and life insurance for employees, spouses, and children. Additionally, all employees are eligible to participate in the South Carolina Retirement System, which offers a defined benefit and defined contribution plan from which to choose as well as voluntary, supplemental 401(k) and 457(b) plans. Each year, our employees enjoy each of the following:
<ul>
<li>23 faculty non-work days per academic year, inclusive of 13 holidays and five additional days for those who choose to work during the summer term (faculty only)</li>
<li>15 days annual leave (staff only)</li>
<li>13 paid holidays (staff only)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>As an integral part of our team, you will play a role in the success of the institution and each of our students. <strong>&ldquo;JOIN US&rdquo; </strong>and make an <strong>IMPACT!</strong></p>
</div><dl class="accordion" data-accordion="">
      <dt class="hidden"></dt><dd class="accordion-navigation active">
    <button aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="item-14442">SEARCH OUR CURRENT JOB OPENINGS</button>
    <div id="item-14442" class="content general-text active">
    	<p><span>We are actively seeking qualified applicants to fill vacant positions as they become available. We accept applications for adjunct faculty on an on-going basis. We accept staff applications only when there is an opening.</span></p>
<p><span>To view our current job openings, you will be directed away from the college website to the </span><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong><a href="https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/fdtc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FDTC Employment Application System</a></strong></span><span>. This online system allows you to search through all available job postings, create an online application, and upload any supporting documents that you wish to include.</span></p>
<p><span>Any questions or comments about any specific position or opening at FDTC should be emailed to employment@fdtc.edu.&nbsp;</span></p>
    </div>
</dd><dd class="accordion-navigation active">
    <button aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="item-14444">APPLICATION PROCESS</button>
    <div id="item-14444" class="content general-text active">
    	<p>To apply to join the FDTC team, <a href="https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/fdtc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">please complete an employment application</a>. Applicants must create a profile and submit application during the advertised vacancy period. During the application process, all questions should be answered completely and all periods of employment and/or unemployment should be included. Please do not leave questions blank unless they do not apply to you, and remember to be specific and accurate in answering all prompts and questions.</p>
<p>If you are applying for more than one position at the same time, an application must be completed for each vacancy. All candidates being considered for hire are subject to a criminal background screening and reference screening.</p>
<p>For positions requiring an Associate Degree, Bachelor&rsquo;s Degree or a Master&rsquo;s Degree, the applicant must attach unofficial transcripts to your online application. (Official transcripts will be obtained at the time of hiring.) If applying for a faculty position, you must include copies of all transcripts. Your application may be excluded from consideration if not completed. <strong>A resume may be attached; however, all sections of the application must be completed. The application must be dated and signed in all requested areas. </strong>The position you are applying for must be noted at the top of the application. Please do not have transcripts mailed directly to the College.</p>
<h4>Interview Committee</h4>
<p>FDTC uses interview committees for all full-time positions. The committee will review applications and identify those to be invited for an interview.</p>
<h4>Interviews</h4>
<p>Applicants selected for an interview will be contacted to schedule an interview. Two or three applicants will be invited for a second interview with the appropriate Vice President, AVP of Human Resources/Internal Relations, and President.</p>
<h4>Hiring</h4>
<p>Job offers are made by the AVP of Human Resources/Internal Relations or designee after conferring with the appropriate Vice President and/or President.</p>
<p>All applicants may be subject to employment history verification. Therefore, it is essential that applicants provide complete information regarding past employment.</p>
    </div>
</dd></dl><span id="d.en.14443"></span>
<div class="general-text">
  
  <p><strong><em>Florence-Darlington Technical College provides equal employment opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability or genetics. In addition to federal law requirements, Florence-Darlington Technical College complies with applicable state and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment in every location in which the company has facilities. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, compensation, and training. Florence-Darlington Technical College expressly prohibits any form of workplace harassment based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, or veteran status.</em></strong></p>
</div><section class="icon-cols">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="small-12 columns text-center">
            <h2 class="header">Still have questions? Contact us!</h2>
            
        </div>

        <div class="icon-col-wrapper icons-3-per-row"><div class="icon-col general-text">
    <img src="/media/fdtc/site-assets/icons/Comunication-icons4.png" alt="" class="icon-image">
    <h3 class="heading">Office Location</h3>
    <p><strong>Human Resources</strong><br />2715 West Lucas St.<br />5000 Building, 2nd Floor</p>
</div><div class="icon-col general-text">
    <img src="/media/fdtc/site-assets/icons/Comunication-icons5.png" alt="" class="icon-image">
    <h3 class="heading">Hours of Operation</h3>
    <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"></span><strong>M - Th:</strong><span> 8:00 am - 5:30 pm</span><br /><strong>F:</strong><span> 8:00 am - 11:30 am</span></p>
</div><div class="icon-col general-text">
    <img src="/media/fdtc/site-assets/icons/Comunication-icons-1.png" alt="" class="icon-image">
    <h3 class="heading">Contact</h3>
